{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391479-conscience-conviction-working-together","id":1391479,"title":"Conscience/Conviction working together?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-25T07:42:55-07:00","id":1391479,"title":"Conscience/Conviction working together?","content":"<br /> So, how I've thought of Conscience is that it's really just <i>ego </i>keeping the beast at bay. I mean it's a resource where you need more of it to get away with bad things; The person that needs 5 dots of Conscience is your murderer/rapist/politician, a good person that does no wrong can work happily with a rating 1 or 2. As a sense of right and wrong, a character's rating is inversely proportional to how good they are, typically. <br /> <br /> But with that logic why does anyone need conviction when it's almost the same thing. Ok, Conviction works a lot better because a high rating and having steadfast beliefs giving you more leeway on the path makes a bit of sense; your beliefs aren't going to crumble because you broke a tenet once or twice. The questionable part is where you can swiftly turn those 4 dots of Road'o Bones conviction into 4 dots of Path of blood conviction. <br /> <br /> Oh, and there are Merits like Code of Honour and king/queen of shadow which just serve to give extra dice to morality rolls....<br /> <br /> <br /> So I was just thinking; What if you had Conscience and Conviction at the same time? <br /> You start with 1 dot in conscience and 0 dots in conviction before you allocate points. <br /> <br /> Assuming you're on a path that asks for Conscience, you use Conscience for morality rolls as normal. However, if you've spent points in Conviction, you gain a number of beliefs and add your conviction rating to morality rolls relevant to your beliefs. You can add your conviction rating to every morality roll related to <i>protecting your honour</i>, or for when you <i>deal with threats</i> or <i>kill in the name of God</i> or <i>protect the masquerade</i> or perhaps when <i>dealing with degenerates.</i> <br /> We can add more to that. Perhaps you must roll your conscience minus your conviction when you act against your convictions. You always have at least one die to roll. <br /> <br /> Now, when you're on a path that asks for Conviction, things get interesting. You normally roll for morality with Conviction, but you keep your Conscience dots; Each one a tether to your former sense of morality. You may be on a monstrous path, but you do not want to lie, cheat, steal, rape, murder. Naturally, this is a weakness in some ways, but the remnants of your former self help stave away the beast in times you might otherwise suffer when stepping off the path. If you break a path tenet, for reasons of conscience, you can add your conscience rating to your conviction for the morality roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T08:33:50-07:00","id":1391487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391479-conscience-conviction-working-together#post1391479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how I've thought of Conscience is that it's really just <i>ego </i>keeping the beast at bay. I mean it's a resource where you need more of it to get away with bad things; The person that needs 5 dots of Conscience is your murderer/rapist/politician, a good person that does no wrong can work happily with a rating 1 or 2. As a sense of right and wrong, a character's rating is inversely proportional to how good they are, typically.</div> </div> </div> </div>remember that you're still supposed to roleplay your stats,<br /> if you have conscience 5 but keep acting as someone that has conscience 0, then you don't have conscience 5<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, when you're on a path that asks for Conviction, things get interesting. You normally roll for morality with Conviction, but you keep your Conscience dots; Each one a tether to your former sense of morality. You may be on a monstrous path, but you do not want to lie, cheat, steal, rape, murder. Naturally, this is a weakness in some ways, </div> </div> </div>it's a weakness in every way,<br /> if you're on the path of Cathari, and you cry everytime you steal, rape, murder,<br /> you're gonna have a hard time advancing on the path,<br /> <br /> it won't prevent degeneration,<br /> on the contrary, you're at higher risk of degenerating, since now you have to roll for failing your convictions, and then you have to roll to see if your conscience acts as a further attack on your morality (or, in the case of Cathari, your immorality)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 05-25-2020, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T09:38:38-07:00","id":1391495,"title":"","content":"Conscience and conviction were totally different in revised. If you had conscience 5, you felt gulity when you broke path sins, you felt bad. Conviction was &quot;I did the Right Thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's why i despaired when they got rolled together, it gave the impression that Humanity could be kept by &quot;Doing the Right Thing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T13:17:13-07:00","id":1391534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391479-conscience-conviction-working-together?p=1391487#post1391487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> it's a weakness in every way,<br /> if you're on the path of Cathari, and you cry everytime you steal, rape, murder,<br /> you're gonna have a hard time advancing on the path,</div> </div> </div> </div>Should clarify, I don't mean you're full on everything humanity when on a path, but that there's something in your conscience that keeps you away from trouble a path normally facilitates. <br /> <br /> For examples<br /> Even though you're on the path of power and the Inner voice, you can't bring yourself to steal. <br /> Despite your devotion to <s>Anarcho Capitalism</s> <b>The Path of Typhon</b>, you can't bring yourself to facilitate pedophilia. The Drugs are fine, adult trafficking is fine, but you just can't bring yourself to work with children. For all the horrors you inflict with the <b>Path of Night</b>, you can't bring yourself to hurt the people you think are truly innocent. <br /> <br /> Specific items. Perhaps there is room for some (higher tennet) path conflicts. For example, Samsara demands you kill vampires who cultivate High humanity for going against their undead Dharma, but perhaps you foolishly believe attempting to achieve high humanity is a valid Dharma, maybe that's just your concious talking. The tennet that demands you kill 'humane' vampires is like, 7th level or something, so quite high. While you don't get to lick your lips and advance the path through hunting high humanity shmucks, you also have a better time justifying not killing your friends when you get to that level. There's a lot of room for players/storytellers to work things out I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:01:58-07:00","id":1391544,"title":"","content":"Somewhat of an aside but looking at the demons of DtF might be interesting to this conversation as demons start with the virtues of Conscience, Conviction, and Courage.<br /> <br /> This is showed that while Conscience handles ethics and morality, one's willingness to do something is instead grounded and their driving Conviction in what they do and what their purpose is to do, so that an interesting phenomena occurs where failure of Self-Control often leads to action while a failure of Conviction often leads to inaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T14:44:21-07:00","id":1391555,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> alright, now I understand","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}